-Hi, Zero.

10:10.280 --> 10:11.200
Hey, Montini.

10:11.800 --> 10:14.080
Another guy who's always at the café.
He lives up there.

10:14.160 --> 10:17.360
-He went to our school as well, remember?
-Yeah, I remember him.

10:17.440 --> 10:19.920
But I only talked to him,
like, twice in five years.

10:20.000 --> 10:23.800
You might think she's exaggerating,
but it was probably even less than that.

10:24.320 --> 10:27.440
My old school had
a very rigid caste system.

10:31.120 --> 10:33.360
People came from India to study it.

10:33.440 --> 10:37.440
To understand how we'd perfected
that model of social segregation.

10:37.520 --> 10:38.680
All through those years,

10:38.760 --> 10:41.440
you could only talk to people
who were exactly as lame as you.

10:41.520 --> 10:44.240
It was a rule. Even the janitors
would beat you up

10:44.320 --> 10:46.720
if they caught you talking
to someone who was better than you.

10:46.800 --> 10:51.480
This impudent boy with dandruff
has dared to lay his eyes on Miss Lavinia!

10:52.720 --> 10:55.360
He's going to feel the whiplash!

10:55.440 --> 10:56.680
And we were lame.

10:56.760 --> 11:00.840
We're talking about the '90s here,
when lame people were really lame!

11:01.440 --> 11:04.080
Cool people would never for a moment
have thought of saying…

11:04.160 --> 11:07.320
Sheldon from
The Big Bang Theory is just like me!

11:07.400 --> 11:10.120
You piece of shit! That is
a bare-faced lie. You know you were cool!

11:10.200 --> 11:11.560
It's like if a Klansman said…

11:11.640 --> 11:16.120
That plantation slave
is just like me when I was young!

11:16.200 --> 11:18.440
But as lame as we indisputably were,

11:18.520 --> 11:22.080
