of being a total reject.

11:24.640 --> 11:27.320
He was the target of any bully's tyranny,

11:27.400 --> 11:30.280
of any arsehole who got out
of the wrong side of the bed.

11:30.360 --> 11:34.840
And it wasn't limited to humans either.
Flora and fauna had it in for him too.

11:34.920 --> 11:38.640
Just to give you an idea, even the pigeons
would shit on his head every break time.

11:38.720 --> 11:41.440
And it wasn't a coincidence either.
It was like some sort of rule.

11:41.520 --> 11:43.440
As if there was a leader pigeon

11:43.520 --> 11:45.680
who'd have a go at the others
if they shat anywhere else.

11:45.760 --> 11:47.200
Hey, guys, come on now.

11:47.280 --> 11:50.240
Is it too much to ask for you
to aim for the toilet when you shit?

11:50.320 --> 11:52.000
I often bring the kids here to eat,

11:52.080 --> 11:55.000
and we're always having to slalom
right through your caca!

11:55.080 --> 11:58.360
Please, now, there's even a sign here.
Shit in the toilet.

11:58.440 --> 12:00.280
Only the toilet was Montini.

12:00.880 --> 12:03.800
So what's he doing now?
Did he find his place in the world?

12:03.880 --> 12:05.440
I felt so sorry for him at school.

12:05.520 --> 12:07.360
I think he's still a bit messed up.

12:07.440 --> 12:09.760
He's always walking around on his own
with that dog.

12:09.840 --> 12:13.040
It's like a rat and wheezes
like my grandpa, who has emphysema.

12:22.240 --> 12:23.760
I really need to tell you why I called…

12:23.840 --> 12:25.440
Whoa, whoa, whoa, hold your horses.

12:25.520 --> 12:28.120
What's up? Do you need to pee?
Are you in some kind of rush?

12:29.240 --> 12:31.120
I need to tell you something
about Wild Boar.

12:31.200 --> 12:32.840
I can't exactly say it outside the café.

12:32.920 --> 12:35.920
Come on, tell me about Wild Boar, then.
What's up with him?

12:36.000 --> 12:38.680
I don't know what's up with him,
but he's in trouble, Sarah.

12:38.760 --> 12:41.200
I don't know how to bring it up
to ask him about it.

12:41.280 --> 12:42.720
What do you mean, in trouble?

12:42.800 --> 12:45.280
He's married with two kids,
and he's still getting into trouble?

12:45.360 --> 12:47.840
If it's about pussy,
I'll go and slap him myself, okay?

12:48.560 --> 12:51.480
-Money keeps going missing.
-What do you mean, going missing?

12:51.560 --> 12:54.520
I don't know. When I look at
the accounts each month, nothing adds up.

12:55.160 --> 12:58.160
It wasn't that much at first. I thought,
"Oh, he must've made a mistake."

12:58.240 --> 13:00.680
But… …it's getting embarrassing now.

13:00.760 --> 13:03.960
And so if you think about
the sheer size of the multiverse

13:04.040 --> 13:08.080
and all the convoluted twists and turns
of fate that brought us to this situation,

13:08.160 --> 13:10.960
when you think of all the possibilities,
it makes your head spin.

13:11.040 --> 13:13.240
And consider the fact
that we're talking about money

13:13.320 --> 13:15.560
that keeps going missing
in bigger and bigger chunks,

13:15.640 --> 13:17.440
that narrows it all right down.

13:17.520 --> 13:19.400
And to top it all off, we're in Rome!

13:19.480 --> 13:22.080
That basically leaves
only one possible explanation.

13:22.160 --> 13:23.560
Okay, so he's a cokehead.

13:23.640 --> 13:26.320
Well, he's not donating it all
to the Waldensian Church

13:26.400 --> 13:27.920
to build a well in Africa.

13:28.000 --> 13:30.080
So, we need to talk to him then, don't we?

13:30.160 --> 13:33.760
Yeah, but I get embarrassed.
What can I say? He's a role model for me.

13:33.840 --> 13:36.360
I don't really think it's my place
to lecture him about stuff.

13:36.440 --> 13:38.040
That's why I wanted us to go together,

13:38.120 --> 13:41.480
so he understands that my problem isn't
that I'm pissed off money's going missing.

13:41.560 --> 13:44.280
It's just that if he's in that state,
he needs help.

13:44.360 --> 13:47.240
Why didn't you give me a call
so we could go and talk to him together?

13:47.320 --> 13:51.840
Well, I did actually tell Secco about it,
then the unfortunate incident happened.

13:51.920 --> 13:53.840
-You know?
-Yeah, I know, of course.

13:53.920 --> 13:57.280
-My heart goes out to Secco.
-Yeah, such a poor guy.

13:58.480 --> 14:01.720
The other day, I walked past his house
and got a lump in my throat.

14:01.800 --> 14:04.200
I could feel that heavy atmosphere.

14:08.880 --> 14:10.800
It's his fault at the end of the day.

14:10.880 --> 14:14.120
Yeah, yeah. But still,
you wouldn't wish that on anyone.

14:14.200 --> 14:16.160
I ended up not talking
to Wild Boar, though.

14:18.040 --> 14:20.120
Well, I'll come along with you now
if you want me to?

14:20.200 --> 14:22.360
Uh, yeah, nice idea,
but maybe another time.

14:22.440 --> 14:24.920
I'm really tired right now.
I can't handle that conversation.

14:25.000 --> 14:27.360
Thanks, though.
At least I could talk to you about it.

14:27.440 --> 14:28.800
I gotta go. Wanna get to bed early.

14:28.880 --> 14:31.600
But I'm glad we had this little chat.
I really needed that.

14:31.680 --> 14:33.560
-Hey, Zero, but…
-Can I call you tomorrow?

14:33.640 --> 14:35.400
Maybe we can have dinner
with Stella as well?

14:35.480 --> 14:37.840
You really are
such a self-centred fuckface, Zero!

14:37.920 --> 14:39.640
You basically did all of the talking!

14:40.280 --> 14:43.760
Uh… I'm not gonna stand for you
calling me a self-centred fuckface.

14:43.840 --> 14:45.760
I think we had a nice
back-and-forth exchange.

14:45.840 --> 14:48.080
-I felt really good vibes.
-What good vibes were they?

14:48.160 --> 14:49.840
Have you got even more stupid?

14:49.920 --> 14:52.480
Do you remember we're meeting
because I asked you to?

14:52.560 --> 14:54.440
I need to tell you something important!

14:55.520 --> 14:57.520
…tell you something important!

14:58.320 --> 15:00.840
Sorry, I, uh,
guess I didn't read that part.

15:00.920 --> 15:03.200
I've developed a psychic blindness
for potential burdens.

15:03.280 --> 15:04.440
I just don't see them.

15:07.040 --> 15:08.680
So then, what's up?

15:08.760 --> 15:11.360
Well, I wanted to ask you
something a bit delicate.

15:11.440 --> 15:13.600
So, first of all, it comes in two parts.

15:13.680 --> 15:16.520
In my head,
when someone is about to ask me something,

15:16.600 --> 15:20.800
the Grand Council of my wisest neurons
gathers to assess the situation.

15:21.320 --> 15:22.560
-Good evening, master.
-Evening.

15:22.640 --> 15:24.600
-How is your prostate?
-Oh, you know.

15:29.280 --> 15:31.560
It's right here, guys.
The request is upon us.

15:32.720 --> 15:34.320
Okay, tell me the first part.

15:34.400 --> 15:38.000
The first part is, I'm going through
a bit of a rough patch with Stella.

15:38.080 --> 15:39.360
A rough patch, you say?

15:39.440 --> 15:41.640
Are you telling me
you broke up for the 670th time?

15:41.720 --> 15:43.920
No, no, Zero, right now we're together.

15:44.000 --> 15:47.000
It's just that we had a bit of a rough
five minutes earlier this morning.

15:47.080 --> 15:49.200
-I hate you!
-You've ruined my life!

15:49.800 --> 15:52.160
Nothing too serious,
but if the trend continues,

15:52.240 --> 15:53.320
we'll break up Friday,

15:53.400 --> 15:55.520
delete each other from social media
on Saturday,

15:55.600 --> 15:57.720
Tuesday, I'll send her a sappy song
on WhatsApp,

15:57.800 --> 16:00.080
and Wednesday,
we'll fuck to get back together.

16:00.880 --> 16:02.760
I must say,
it sounds like a weather forecast.

16:02.840 --> 16:04.680
Yeah, and I've got this app

16:04.760 --> 16:06.400
that tells you all your fights day by day,

16:06.480 --> 16:08.800
like the one that helps you
lose 44 pounds in a month.

16:08.880 --> 16:10.600
Don't worry, guys. It's not a burden.

16:10.680 --> 16:13.400
Sentimental confessions.
I repeat, sentimental confessions.

16:13.480 --> 16:15.600
Open the gate, Hector!

16:17.520 --> 16:20.400
Okay, but you two have been doing this
for years, right?

16:20.480 --> 16:22.920
I thought this was
some sort of harmony for you.

16:23.000 --> 16:24.040
Yeah, but the thing is,

16:24.120 --> 16:26.200
a friend of mine had a fight
with her boyfriend.

16:26.280 --> 16:28.400
She's asked if she can come stay with us

16:28.480 --> 16:30.800
because things have got really bad
at home for her.

16:30.880 --> 16:32.120
Her fella's a piece of shit.

16:32.200 --> 16:37.280
I don't know him, Zero, but she's told me
some really bad things. He hit her.

16:37.360 --> 16:39.360
I can hardly leave her on the street,
can I?

16:39.440 --> 16:41.680
And I sure can't send her back to him.

16:41.760 --> 16:43.640
Long live Sarah! Hooray!

16:43.720 --> 16:46.680
'Cause she's a jolly good fellow
'Cause she's a jolly good fellow

16:46.760 --> 16:49.120
You are fantastic
for taking her in, sister.

16:49.200 --> 16:51.680
-That piece of excrement!
-Tell us where he lives. We'll get him!

16:51.760 --> 16:54.480
Well. That is a shitty situation.
How's she doing?

16:55.120 --> 16:56.960
Well, she really is in a right mess,

16:57.040 --> 17:00.920
but it's all a bit complicated at home
with Stella at the moment, you know?

17:01.000 --> 17:03.040
What's the connection
between Stella and your friend?

17:03.120 --> 17:06.720
Well, there isn't one. I just don't wanna
upset a very delicate equilibrium,

17:06.800 --> 17:10.080
'cause things are so fragile,
and she needs a quiet place right now.

17:10.680 --> 17:12.880
What the fuck is she asking me?

17:12.960 --> 17:16.760
Eeny, meeny, miney, moe

17:17.280 --> 17:19.160
The castle has been breached!

17:19.240 --> 17:22.680
We were foolish. Sound the alarm.
I'm gonna piss myself.

17:22.760 --> 17:26.520
So, basically, just for a few days,
that's all, if you could, Zero…

17:26.600 --> 17:33.440
Let her stay.

17:35.600 --> 17:37.200
Oh, come on, you utter piece of shit.

17:37.280 --> 17:40.920
You're dumping this on me because you knew
that I'd feel guilty. Damn you, Sarah!

17:41.000 --> 17:42.480
Well, yeah, you got me there.

17:43.000 --> 17:45.120
But that's always how it works
with you anyway.

17:45.200 --> 17:48.160
We don't talk to you directly,
but to your sense of guilt.

17:48.240 --> 17:49.800
We skip you out altogether.

17:49.880 --> 17:51.600
Look, don't you worry. I'll talk to him.

17:51.680 --> 17:54.480
He'll do whatever I tell him to.
He's just a puppet.

17:54.560 --> 17:57.640
Hang on now, Sarah.
Think about her for a moment, would you?

17:57.720 --> 17:59.400
I can't let a stranger into my house.

17:59.480 --> 18:02.440
Wait, this is the second part,
and it's a little bit shorter.

18:02.520 --> 18:05.160
-She's not technically a stranger.
-Hey, Zeh.

18:07.040 --> 18:09.600
Has this smartarse
already dropped the bomb?

18:09.680 --> 18:10.960
Smeralda?

18:12.400 --> 18:15.240
-Oh, my diapers!
-Stay with me, Mario!

18:15.320 --> 18:17.560
Okay, guys. It's Smeralda.

18:17.640 --> 18:21.120
Gentlemen, it was a real pleasure
working with you all. Adieu.

18:27.400 --> 18:31.120
Bless his little heart, he's in shock.
Now, you don't have to say yes, Zeh.

18:31.200 --> 18:33.600
Honestly, I did tell Sarah
it was a bit of an imposition.

18:33.680 --> 18:36.520
What are you on about, girl?
This arse has a massive house.

18:36.600 --> 18:38.520
He has a room for his plastic alligator.

18:38.600 --> 18:41.560
All right, leave Rosario out of this.
He needs his space.

18:42.520 --> 18:43.760
I wish I'd said…

18:43.840 --> 18:45.320
"Let's swap houses for a few days."

18:45.400 --> 18:47.560
"I'll leave you my place,
but you take care of all this."

18:47.640 --> 18:50.560
But I didn't, 'cause I know what it's like
being with Sarah and Stella.

18:50.640 --> 18:53.920
We went on a road trip last year.
They started fighting after 20 minutes.

18:54.000 --> 18:55.760
I was in the back looking out the window,

18:55.840 --> 18:58.880
and I thought that if Shenron the Dragon
suddenly appeared from behind the hill

18:58.960 --> 19:01.760
and could grant me one wish,
I'd want to be a worm,

19:01.840 --> 19:04.600
or at least one of those animals
that can't hear or see anything

19:04.680 --> 19:06.840
and only relates to the world
through touch.

19:08.600 --> 19:11.880
Instead, I still had all my senses,
so I could hear them screaming.

19:11.960 --> 19:13.680
I just wanted to disappear
into the car seat

19:13.760 --> 19:15.280
because I felt so embarrassed.

19:15.360 --> 19:18.880
I tried to act casual and kept scrolling
through my phone, but then it died,

19:18.960 --> 19:21.560
so I started looking intently
at the seams of the seats

19:21.640 --> 19:23.800
and pretended to be very interested,

19:23.880 --> 19:25.800
when I was actually
sitting there thinking…

19:25.880 --> 19:29.000
How the actual fuck can you two fight
in front of other people?

19:29.080 --> 19:31.880
I have nothing against people who fight.
I have many friends who fight.

19:31.960 --> 19:33.120
As long as they do it at home

19:33.200 --> 19:35.280
and don't flaunt it
in front of my inner child,

19:35.360 --> 19:37.040
who doesn't wanna see certain things.

19:37.120 --> 19:38.760
Besides, I'm very judgmental,

19:38.840 --> 19:41.680
so I had to bite my tongue
a hundred times to not tell Sarah…

19:41.760 --> 19:44.000
What, are you deaf!
What the hell's wrong with you?

19:44.080 --> 19:46.440
Come on, Sarah!
You can't let her treat you like that.

19:46.520 --> 19:48.880
But then she turned around and said…

19:48.960 --> 19:51.160
I'm really sorry you had to witness this.

19:52.160 --> 19:55.560
And honestly,
I couldn't hold it in any more, so I said…

19:56.080 --> 19:58.760
Oh, were you two fighting?
I wasn't listening at all.

19:58.840 --> 20:01.680
I was utterly absorbed
in looking at this stitching.

20:01.760 --> 20:05.000
This really is
wonderful Italian craftsmanship.

20:05.520 --> 20:08.120
So, yeah,
I would've spared Smeralda from that.

20:08.720 --> 20:10.920
Anyway, this idiot didn't tell me
it was you,

20:11.000 --> 20:13.240
otherwise there is no way
I would've said all those things.

20:13.320 --> 20:15.200
So, what the fuck is going on?

20:15.280 --> 20:17.720
Well, I don't quite know
what Sarah's told you, Zeh,

20:17.800 --> 20:21.120
but I'm in a bit of a state.
I just think I need a change of scenery.

20:22.640 --> 20:25.600
That's funny, you've always struck me
as a very level-headed person

20:25.680 --> 20:29.000
with razor-sharp surgical precision
whenever it comes to judging people.

20:29.080 --> 20:32.080
Can I say, that sounds
very weird coming from you.

20:32.160 --> 20:35.920
You don't exactly have a reputation for
surrounding yourself with stable people.

20:36.000 --> 20:38.600
-I don't understand…
-You are a true diviner of cringe.

20:38.680 --> 20:41.120
You go searching for it with a stick.

20:42.720 --> 20:44.600
You're completely wrong. I'm not…

20:44.680 --> 20:47.040
Can you shut up now, please?
Let's move on now.

20:47.120 --> 20:49.080
Or this episode will never fucking end.

20:49.160 --> 20:53.240
I have a lot of faith in humanity. I like
to bet on people's hidden qualities.

20:53.320 --> 20:55.080
So, are you gonna let us stay or not?

20:55.160 --> 20:57.320
I have a line of people waiting.
I don't need to beg.

20:57.400 --> 21:00.520
What is "us" supposed to mean?
Come on, tell me. Us who?

21:00.600 --> 21:02.280
You and your 450 personalities?

21:02.360 --> 21:05.560
Don't tell me you've got a kid,
or I swear I'll kill myself.

21:05.640 --> 21:07.920
-Oh, didn't Sarah tell you?
-Mm-mm.

21:08.920 --> 21:09.760
Macchiato!

21:19.080 --> 21:22.440
Sarah, for fuck's sake.
You're saddling me with a zoo.

21:22.520 --> 21:24.640
Oh, come on now. He's such good boy.

21:24.720 --> 21:27.600
Even the cat bullied him at my place.
Isn't that right?

21:28.200 --> 21:29.440
Right, Macchiato?

21:29.520 --> 21:32.600
So submissive in a house full of women!

21:33.120 --> 21:35.120
So, what are you going to do, Zero?

21:35.200 --> 21:36.720
What's there to decide?

21:36.800 --> 21:38.880
She's running away
from a guy who beats her up.

21:38.960 --> 21:41.880
You've known this woman forever.
You even have a guest room.

21:41.960 --> 21:43.520
How can you possibly think of saying no?

21:43.600 --> 21:45.560
What did they teach you,
your mother, your father,

21:45.640 --> 21:49.480
Dragon Shiryu, Master Yoda,
Kenshiro, Nelson Mandela, Max Pezzali,

21:49.560 --> 21:53.760
those who tried to give two cents' worth
of values to you, did you not heed them?

21:53.840 --> 21:56.440
They'd spit in your face
if you don't let her stay.

21:59.240 --> 22:02.200
So, then? What are you gonna do?

22:02.280 --> 22:04.360
All right, but tomorrow, I beg you.

22:04.440 --> 22:07.440
Can you just let me have
one last night as a free man?

22:08.880 --> 22:10.880
Thank you, Zeh. I owe you one.

22:10.960 --> 22:13.400
Sorry, but how long exactly
are we talking about?

22:13.480 --> 22:16.360
Not long, I promise. I'll get the hell out
before you tire of me.

22:16.440 --> 22:17.400
But I hope you don't.

22:17.480 --> 22:19.200
So, let's have a chat tomorrow,

22:19.280 --> 22:22.240
and we can agree on
when I can deliver this lovely bundle.

22:24.760 --> 22:27.560
I can't believe you still blush
like when you were 12 years old!

22:27.640 --> 22:29.400
You really are such a fucking dumbarse!

22:34.080 --> 22:37.600
BYE, CATERPILLAR

22:40.160 --> 22:41.200
CRAZY PIZZA

22:51.200 --> 22:52.760
THE ETERNAL SUNSHINE
OF THE BOO-HOO MIND

23:28.680 --> 23:32.160
You know deep down you didn't accept
just out of a sense of guilt, right?

23:32.680 --> 23:35.200
Look, it's only 'cause
she's in a shitty situation at the moment.

23:35.280 --> 23:36.480
You are a liar.

23:36.560 --> 23:39.320
And not even like a Jesuit,
like a silo full of Jesuits.

23:39.400 --> 23:41.680
What was I supposed to say
when she was standing there?

23:41.760 --> 23:43.800
I'm not judging you.
I'm not saying anything.

23:43.880 --> 23:47.160
Just don't bust my balls later
'cause I'll give you what's coming to you.

23:49.280 --> 23:52.040
Hey, have you noticed
that in your pantheon of role models,

23:52.120 --> 23:54.920
apart from your mother, they are all men?

23:55.000 --> 23:58.920
This time around, Netflix will send you
to a re-education camp in Siberia.

24:02.800 --> 24:04.520
What's that got to do with anything?

24:04.600 --> 24:06.280
I was born in the '80s.
There was no Eleven,

24:06.360 --> 24:08.640
no Handmaid's Tale,
and all that cool stuff.

24:08.720 --> 24:11.520
Back then, girls in cartoons
were dainty cry-babies.

24:11.600 --> 24:14.440
What kinda fucking role models were they?

24:14.520 --> 24:16.560
And what about The Rose of Versailles?

24:24.880 --> 24:26.440
Toxic masculinity.

24:27.400 --> 24:29.040
Oh, how I cried.

24:29.120 --> 24:32.360
I wept buckets
when André banged her down by the Seine.

24:32.440 --> 24:34.120
I couldn't sleep for three nights.

24:43.680 --> 24:45.160
Hey, dude! Where were you?

24:45.240 --> 24:47.480
That Smeralda came here
looking for you earlier.

24:47.560 --> 24:49.120
Yeah, I ran into her outside.

24:49.200 --> 24:50.960
She says she's coming to stay.

24:51.040 --> 24:54.480
-What am I supposed to do with her?
-Maybe you'll finally go all the way.

24:54.560 --> 24:56.960
Gimme that one satisfaction
after 20 years.

24:57.040 --> 24:58.520
What did we make you go to school for?

24:58.600 --> 25:00.520
Oh, forget it.
She's not coming for a holiday.

25:00.600 --> 25:02.240
She's got a whole lot of stuff going on.

25:02.320 --> 25:04.440
So what? When, in the history of humanity,

25:04.520 --> 25:06.880
have people stopped porking
'cause they had stuff going on?

25:06.960 --> 25:08.040
Look at the baby boom.

25:09.080 --> 25:11.360
I look at him and think, "You bastard."

25:11.440 --> 25:15.000
"You're still screwing around instead
of telling me what the hell you're up to."

25:15.080 --> 25:16.160
You make that face

25:16.240 --> 25:19.160
'cause all you think I am
is a yokel from Sulmona.

25:19.240 --> 25:21.520
But it's not me saying it.
History says so!

25:22.320 --> 25:24.520
My grandfather's uncle
lived near the coast

25:24.600 --> 25:26.240
when the Normans were raiding.

25:26.320 --> 25:28.440
And do you know
what his father used to tell him?

25:28.520 --> 25:30.520
Hang on.
I think you got the dates mixed up.

25:30.600 --> 25:34.360
My son, I understand you're getting
very worried about the Normans.

25:34.440 --> 25:37.240
The dog will take care of them.
He'll bark if he sees them.

25:38.680 --> 25:40.080
You only have to do one thing.

25:40.160 --> 25:41.800
You need to get laid!

25:43.400 --> 25:44.920
See why I can't talk to him?

25:45.000 --> 25:48.080
I can't say, "Hey, sit down,
and we can talk about your problem."

25:48.160 --> 25:50.040
Because he's always been like that.

25:50.120 --> 25:52.040
You might think he's a fuckwit,

25:52.120 --> 25:54.520
but he was the fuckwit
who knew more than any of us.

25:55.120 --> 25:58.680
The one who gave you advice
because he had more experience than you.

25:59.200 --> 26:03.280
All the things that make you
the alpha male in the male hierarchy.

26:04.760 --> 26:07.960
Remember what I said
about the caste system at my school?

26:08.040 --> 26:09.040
Well,

26:09.840 --> 26:11.600
Wild Boar was the only one

26:11.680 --> 26:14.400
who could switch
from one caste to another.

26:17.600 --> 26:20.040
He'd hang out with us lame guys
in the morning,

26:20.120 --> 26:22.760
and then, in the afternoon,
he'd go out with Monica,

26:22.840 --> 26:25.040
who was at the top of the social pyramid.

26:25.120 --> 26:28.120
Then, before dinner,
he'd come back to us in the arcade

26:28.200 --> 26:30.480
and tell us how shiny the world above was.

26:31.000 --> 26:32.760
He was like the Dune Messiah,

26:32.840 --> 26:35.240
the one who could walk between two worlds.

26:35.320 --> 26:38.480
Lisan al-Gaib! Lisan al-Gaib!

26:40.400 --> 26:44.520
On the day he married Christine,
we thought he'd finally grown up.

26:48.360 --> 26:51.840
But no. He was still showing off
and talking down to us.

26:51.920 --> 26:52.960
Saying things like…

26:53.040 --> 26:56.080
Well, you guys are just kids.
I'll explain when you grow up.

26:57.000 --> 27:00.480
The thing is, after all these years
of him being the Messiah

27:00.560 --> 27:03.280
and us being his disciples,
how can you one day say…

27:03.360 --> 27:04.800
Hey, bro, that's enough.

27:04.880 --> 27:06.800
You were so good
at getting laid back then,

27:06.880 --> 27:09.800
but you're getting desperate right now.
You're hooked on this stuff.

27:09.880 --> 27:11.880
And now it falls upon us to help you.

27:11.960 --> 27:14.360
Us, the lame guys
who hung on your every word.

27:14.880 --> 27:18.440
It's humiliating for him,
and we'd have to throw away this script

27:19.280 --> 27:22.320
and stop playing these roles
we've always played.

27:22.400 --> 27:25.560
And that scares me,
because I don't know how to live

27:25.640 --> 27:28.720
without someone to reassure me
and tell me I'm doing okay.

27:32.560 --> 27:34.920
We'll feel the same

27:35.000 --> 27:39.680
Well, no one knows…

27:39.760 --> 27:42.480
If we step out of the comfort zone
of this little theatre,

27:42.560 --> 27:44.400
of us being here on this lit stage,

27:44.480 --> 27:46.200
I don't know what's out there.

27:46.280 --> 27:48.280
It's all dark. You can't see anything.

27:50.160 --> 27:56.080
I just want to be me

27:57.600 --> 27:59.320
And when I can

28:00.960 --> 28:03.080
I will

28:05.000 --> 28:09.560
Try to understand

28:10.600 --> 28:12.400
That when I can…

28:12.480 --> 28:15.920
I don't know
where the fuck we're going. Blindly.

28:19.240 --> 28:22.120
But it's not a problem
because, suddenly, he tells me…

28:22.200 --> 28:24.680
You didn't see me tonight, Zero, okay?
I'll explain later.

28:24.760 --> 28:25.600
What do you mean?

28:25.680 --> 28:27.560
I'll explain later! I'll explain later!

28:28.320 --> 28:30.120
I didn't understand what he was saying.

28:30.200 --> 28:31.800
He seemed like a complete idiot.

28:31.880 --> 28:35.520
Until I heard that bell.

28:40.760 --> 28:41.880
Good evening.

28:45.440 --> 28:46.720
Carlito.

28:51.920 --> 28:52.880
Miss.

28:55.440 --> 28:59.120
Hey, sweet lullaby

28:59.200 --> 29:01.920
Where have you gone?

29:02.000 --> 29:04.320
I wanna love you…

29:04.400 --> 29:05.640
Do we know each other?

29:05.720 --> 29:07.920
Damn right we know each other!

29:08.000 --> 29:09.640
You are Tripwire.

29:10.480 --> 29:11.640
TRIPWIRE

29:11.720 --> 29:15.840
An expert in Japanese katana,
a highly esteemed cocaine addict,

29:15.920 --> 29:19.480
and a champion of that practice
that no one called bullying at the time,

29:19.560 --> 29:23.280
just "I'll beat you to a pulp.
And you know why? Because I can!"

29:23.360 --> 29:25.760
And we all sucked it up
because in the '80s,

29:25.840 --> 29:27.920
the greatest luminary
of developmental psychology

29:28.000 --> 29:29.440
was Charles Darwin.

29:29.520 --> 29:31.640
NATURAL SELECTION
MONTESSORI SUCKS

29:31.720 --> 29:34.240
For decades,
he was the terror of East Rome.

29:34.320 --> 29:37.920
He doesn't remember us
because we were all potential prey to him.

29:38.000 --> 29:41.320
Practically everyone in his field
of vision was potential prey.

29:41.840 --> 29:43.200
A bit less now, though,

29:43.280 --> 29:45.400
because he moved to Dicksville
through a promotion,

29:45.480 --> 29:47.920
and it's not a field
you can work in remotely.

29:51.720 --> 29:53.480
Uh, I don't think we know each other.

29:56.320 --> 29:57.960
I'm looking for the warthog.

29:58.040 --> 29:59.760
I'm afraid he's not here tonight.

30:00.560 --> 30:03.080
So this place stays open on its own?

30:04.120 --> 30:06.720
I'm here. I'm his friend.
You can leave him a message.

30:09.560 --> 30:12.240
I don't have to tell him anything.
Don't you worry.

30:12.320 --> 30:15.880
I'm gonna take a quick look
at the kitchen. I wanna open a café too.

30:15.960 --> 30:17.440
You can't go in there.

30:17.520 --> 30:19.200
Thanks. I'll be quick.

30:30.960 --> 30:33.320
The hog didn't come in to work his shift?

30:33.400 --> 30:35.280
Oh no, these days,
he's not here very often.

30:35.360 --> 30:36.800
I don't know when he'll be back.

30:36.880 --> 30:38.600
He really doesn't like to do shit.

30:38.680 --> 30:41.800
No, he does actually work here
quite a lot. It's just recently that he's…

30:41.880 --> 30:45.240
It's not good when you have a friend
who doesn't like to do shit.

30:46.280 --> 30:48.960
Because his problems become your problems.

30:49.480 --> 30:52.880
Yeah, it's really not good.

30:52.960 --> 30:54.600
I'm sorry, but what problems?

30:58.160 --> 31:00.120
Anyway, have a nice evening.

31:01.360 --> 31:04.680
I'll be sure to tell him you swung by.
What is your name?

31:07.320 --> 31:10.760
No names. You can just tell him
Dicksville stopped by.

31:11.360 --> 31:15.080
Hey, you tool, give me a ride home.
You were leaving anyway, right?

31:15.160 --> 31:16.960
But I live just there!

31:17.040 --> 31:19.640
Well, you can take a ride.
Buy some cigarettes.

31:19.720 --> 31:23.480
-But my car is parked far away, though.
-Go get it. I'll wait right here.

31:23.560 --> 31:25.000
I want God to come

31:26.800 --> 31:28.240
And take me home…

31:28.320 --> 31:30.680
-I live just there, though!
-'Cause I'm all alone…

31:32.280 --> 31:34.480
In this crowd

31:36.240 --> 31:38.520
Who are you to me?

31:39.640 --> 31:42.080
Who am I supposed to be?

31:43.000 --> 31:47.840
Not exactly sure any more

31:49.800 --> 31:52.200
Where's this going to?

31:52.960 --> 31:55.560
Can I follow through?

31:56.280 --> 31:58.760
Or just follow you

31:59.520 --> 32:01.760
For a while?

32:02.840 --> 32:08.040
Does anyone ever get this right?

32:08.120 --> 32:10.760
-Hey, come out. Jeez!
-I feel…

32:10.840 --> 32:13.520
Now, what the actual fuck are you up to?

32:14.360 --> 32:16.400
Don't say a word to Christine!

32:19.800 --> 32:24.760
GOODBYE LORENZO 2004 - 2025
